---
/**
 * /personal-finance-guide
 *
 * Angle: Beginners, simplicity seekers, overwhelmed users
 * Audience: People new to personal finance or frustrated by complex apps
 * Intent: "I want something simple to manage my money"
 *
 * Target Keywords:
 * - personal finance guide (100-1K)
 * - personal finance for beginners (100-1K)
 * - budgeting for beginners (1K-10K)
 * - simple budgeting app (1K-10K)
 * - how to manage personal finances (100-1K)
 * - budgeting made simple (100-1K)
 * - easy budgeting app (100-1K)
 */

import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { pages, APP_URL, SITE_URL } from '@/data/pages';
import AngleHero from '@/components/AngleHero.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import FeatureList from '@/components/FeatureList.astro';
import CTABlock from '@/components/CTABlock.astro';
import SiblingLinks from '@/components/SiblingLinks.astro';

const meta = pages.personalFinanceGuide;

// Ring stats for "The overwhelm problem" section
const R = 48;
const C = 2 * Math.PI * R;
const overwhelmRings = [
  { pct: 77, label: 'of Americans experience "significant" stress over money' },
  { pct: 28, label: 'of households have a written financial plan' },
  { pct: 57, label: 'of Americans spend more than they earn' },
].map(({ pct, label }) => ({ pct, label, offset: C * (1 - pct / 100) }));

const faqSchema = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: "How do I start managing my personal finances if I've never done it before?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "Start by tracking your spending for one week. Don't change anything yet, just write down every transaction. This reveals where your money actually goes, not where you think it goes. Once you see patterns, create 5-6 broad budget categories (housing, food, transport, entertainment, savings). Set realistic limits based on what you learned. The biggest beginner mistake is trying to track 30+ categories from day one. Start simple, add complexity only when you need it."
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Why do I always run out of money before payday?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "Living paycheck to paycheck usually means one of three things: you're spending more than you earn, you're not accounting for irregular expenses (insurance, gifts, annual subscriptions), or you lack visibility into where money actually goes. Small daily purchases add up invisibly - that $6 coffee becomes $180/month, $2,160/year. Track every transaction for one month. Most people discover $200-400 in \"leakage\" they didn't realize existed. Then budget for irregular expenses by setting aside money monthly - if car insurance costs $600/year, save $50/month so it's not a surprise. Cash flow tracking shows exactly how long your money lasts and where the gaps are."
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'How much should I save before I start investing?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "Don't invest until you have 3-6 months of expenses saved in an emergency fund. This isn't being conservative - it's preventing disaster. Without liquidity, the first emergency (car repair, medical bill, job loss) forces you to sell investments at the worst possible time or rack up high-interest credit card debt. The order matters: build a starter emergency fund ($1,000), kill high-interest debt (anything over 6-8%), then complete your emergency fund, then invest. Investing while carrying 20% APR credit card debt is like filling a bathtub with the drain open. Track your net worth to see both emergency funds and investments grow together - they're different tools serving different purposes."
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: "What's the difference between good debt and bad debt?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "\"Good\" debt has three characteristics: low interest rate (under 4-6%), builds equity or income potential (mortgage, student loans for in-demand careers), and the asset typically appreciates or generates returns. \"Bad\" debt is high-interest (credit cards at 15-25%), used for depreciating assets (new cars, consumer goods), and drains your monthly cash flow. The real test: can the thing you're borrowing for generate more value than the interest cost? A mortgage at 3.5% on a home that appreciates is mathematically sound. A credit card at 22% for clothes or dining out is financially destructive. Track your debts alongside your net worth - seeing the interest pile up monthly is a powerful motivator to eliminate it. Prioritize paying down anything over 6-8% before investing excess income."
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: "How do I stop overspending on things I don't need?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "Overspending happens when spending is invisible or emotional. The solution is friction and awareness. Use envelope budgeting - allocate fixed amounts to categories, and when the envelope is empty, you're done for the month. This forces conscious decisions: \"Do I really want this, or do I want to save this budget for something better?\" Implement a 48-hour rule for non-essential purchases over $50. Write them down, wait two days, then decide. Most impulse purchases lose their appeal quickly. Manual transaction tracking (not automatic bank sync) creates natural friction - logging every purchase makes you confront spending patterns. When you have to write \"$47 - impulse Amazon order\" into your budget, you start questioning whether it was worth it."
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Do I really need to track every single expense?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: "Yes, if you want to actually understand your finances. The small stuff matters - it's not about the $3 coffee, it's about realizing you spent $90 this month on coffee without noticing. Untracked spending is invisible spending, and invisible spending is where budgets fail. You can't manage what you don't measure. The good news: it takes 30 seconds per transaction. Log it when you spend it, not at the end of the week from memory. That daily ritual of recording transactions creates mindfulness - you become conscious of spending patterns instead of wondering where your money went. After 2-3 months, tracking becomes automatic habit, and your budget reflects reality instead of wishful thinking. Most people find $200-400/month in spending they didn't realize was happening."
      }
    }
  ]
});
---

<Layout
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  canonical={`/${meta.slug}`}
  ogImage={meta.ogImage}
>

  {/* WebPage schema for rich results and crawl clarity */}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'WebPage',
      name: meta.title,
      description: meta.description,
      url: `${SITE_URL}/${meta.slug}`,
    })}
  </script>

  {/* BreadcrumbList schema for SERP breadcrumbs */}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: SITE_URL },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Personal Finance Guide', item: `${SITE_URL}/${meta.slug}` },
      ],
    })}
  </script>

  {/* FAQPage schema for FAQ rich results */}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqSchema} />

  <AngleHero
    eyebrow="Personal Finance Made Simple"
    title="Personal Finance: A Complete Guide"
    subtitle="Understand your money, build better habits, and take control. Everything you need to know about personal finance."
    keyword="personal finance for beginners"
    showCta={false}
  />

  <!-- Wrapper: full width, clip horizontal overflow only. Inner uses left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 so image stays centered when wider than viewport (e.g. ~768–1100px). -->
  <div class="w-full overflow-x-clip -mt-56 md:-mt-96 mb-0 relative z-10">
    <div class="relative left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-full md:w-max">
      <div class="hero-image-reveal w-full min-w-0 shrink-0 md:w-max">
        <!-- Mobile: fit viewport then scale up just a little (1.08). Desktop: fixed width. -->
        <div class="origin-center scale-[1.3] md:scale-100 w-full md:w-[1120px] md:max-w-none">
        <img
          src="/images/personal-finance-guide/hero_light.png"
          alt="Personal finance guide — simple money management"
          class="w-auto max-w-full md:w-full h-auto rounded-lg block dark:hidden"
        />
        <img
          src="/images/personal-finance-guide/hero_dark.png"
          alt="Personal finance guide — simple money management"
          class="w-auto max-w-full md:w-full h-auto rounded-lg block hidden dark:block"
        />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       SECTION 1: Money skills anyone can learn
       ============================================================ -->
  <Section
    heading="Money skills anyone can learn"
    bg="stone"
    class="mt-0 md:-mt-2 !pt-10 md:!pt-1"
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start md:gap-8 lg:gap-10">
      <!-- Text column (left on desktop) -->
      <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 max-w-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Personal finance doesn't require a degree in economics. At its core, it's about three things: knowing where your money goes, spending less than you earn, and putting the difference to work. That's it.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Most people struggle not because personal finance is complicated, but because they don't have a plan. A simple budget and an investment strategy - that's what makes the difference.
        </p>
        <!-- Mobile only: after second paragraph. Hidden under 450px; >=450px float right; <450px in line (but hidden) -->
        <div class="rocks-reveal md:hidden max-[449px]:hidden mb-4 min-[380px]:float-right min-[380px]:ml-4 min-[380px]:mb-4 min-[380px]:mt-0 w-fit">
          <img
            src="/images/personal-finance-guide/piggy_bank.png"
            alt="Simple personal finance — no complexity"
            class="rounded-lg max-w-[140px] min-[380px]:max-w-[160px] mx-auto min-[380px]:mx-0 block"
          />
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg font-medium text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed mb-0">
          This guide breaks down everything you should know about managing your money.
        </p>
        <div class="clear-both md:clear-none"></div>
      </div>
      <!-- Image: right column on desktop only -->
      <div class="rocks-reveal hidden md:block flex-shrink-0 w-full md:max-w-[270px] lg:max-w-[270px] p-6 lg:p-8">
        <img
          src="/images/personal-finance-guide/piggy_bank.png"
          alt="Simple personal finance — no complexity"
          class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       SECTION 2: THREE THINGS THAT ACTUALLY MATTER
       ============================================================ -->
  <Section
    heading="Three things that actually matter"
    align="center"
  >
    <div class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 md:gap-6">
      <!-- Card 1: Liquidity -->
      <div class="habit-card rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 transition-transform duration-200 hover:-translate-y-1 shadow-[8px_8px_16px_rgba(0,0,0,0.08),-4px_-4px_12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[8px_8px_18px_rgba(0,0,0,0.5),10px_10px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12),-3px_-3px_6px_rgba(255,255,255,0.08)] flex flex-col items-center text-center">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 flex items-center justify-center mb-4 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 2v20M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-2">Liquidity</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
          Going broke can often be a timing issue. A budget shows where your money goes, and an emergency fund keeps you afloat when life happens.
        </p>
      </div>
      <!-- Card 2: Investing -->
      <div class="habit-card rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 transition-transform duration-200 hover:-translate-y-1 shadow-[8px_8px_16px_rgba(0,0,0,0.08),-4px_-4px_12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[8px_8px_18px_rgba(0,0,0,0.5),10px_10px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12),-3px_-3px_6px_rgba(255,255,255,0.08)] flex flex-col items-center text-center">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 flex items-center justify-center mb-4 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M3 3v18h18"/>
            <path d="M7 14l4-4 4 4 5-8"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-2">Investing</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
          Don't pay management fees. Low-cost index funds beat most active managers. Build a simple portfolio, automate it, and let compound growth work.
        </p>
      </div>
      <!-- Card 3: Stability -->
      <div class="habit-card rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 transition-transform duration-200 hover:-translate-y-1 shadow-[8px_8px_16px_rgba(0,0,0,0.08),-4px_-4px_12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[8px_8px_18px_rgba(0,0,0,0.5),10px_10px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12),-3px_-3px_6px_rgba(255,255,255,0.08)] flex flex-col items-center text-center">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 flex items-center justify-center mb-4 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-2">Stability</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
          Don't let debt or disaster wipe you out. Kill high-interest debt first, get essential insurance coverage, and protect the wealth you've built.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       SECTION 2B: GETTING STARTED CHECKLIST
       ============================================================ -->
  <Section
    heading="The personal finance to-do list"
    subheading="How many of these have you covered?"
    align="center"
    class="getting-started-section"
  >
    <div class="checklist-container max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <div class="checklist-item border-b border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 py-5 flex items-start gap-4" data-step="1">
        <label class="checkbox-wrapper flex-shrink-0 cursor-pointer">
          <input type="checkbox" class="checklist-checkbox sr-only">
          <span class="checkbox-custom w-6 h-6 rounded border-2 border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 flex items-center justify-center transition-all duration-200 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900">
            <svg class="checkmark w-4 h-4 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M3 8l3 3 7-7"/>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </label>
        <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
          <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">1. Set up a budget tracking system</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">Choose an app or spreadsheet to track expenses. Start logging where your money goes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item border-b border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 py-5 flex items-start gap-4" data-step="2">
        <label class="checkbox-wrapper flex-shrink-0 cursor-pointer">
          <input type="checkbox" class="checklist-checkbox sr-only">
          <span class="checkbox-custom w-6 h-6 rounded border-2 border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 flex items-center justify-center transition-all duration-200 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900">
            <svg class="checkmark w-4 h-4 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M3 8l3 3 7-7"/>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </label>
        <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
          <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">2. Build your emergency fund</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">Save 3 months of expenses in a high-yield savings account. This is your financial safety net.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item border-b border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 py-5 flex items-start gap-4" data-step="3">
        <label class="checkbox-wrapper flex-shrink-0 cursor-pointer">
          <input type="checkbox" class="checklist-checkbox sr-only">
          <span class="checkbox-custom w-6 h-6 rounded border-2 border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 flex items-center justify-center transition-all duration-200 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900">
            <svg class="checkmark w-4 h-4 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M3 8l3 3 7-7"/>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </label>
        <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
          <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">3. Pay down bad debts</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">Anything over 4% is considered high interest. Don't let it compound against you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-item py-5 flex items-start gap-4" data-step="4">
        <label class="checkbox-wrapper flex-shrink-0 cursor-pointer">
          <input type="checkbox" class="checklist-checkbox sr-only">
          <span class="checkbox-custom w-6 h-6 rounded border-2 border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-600 flex items-center justify-center transition-all duration-200 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900">
            <svg class="checkmark w-4 h-4 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M3 8l3 3 7-7"/>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </label>
        <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
          <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">4. Build an investment portfolio</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">Invest excess capital in a diversified portfolio to grow wealth and combat inflation. </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <script>
      (function () {
        const STORAGE_KEY = 'pf-checklist-state';
        const container = document.querySelector('.checklist-container');
        if (!container) return;

        const items = container.querySelectorAll('.checklist-item');

        // Load saved state from localStorage
        function loadState() {
          try {
            const saved = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);
            if (saved) {
              const state = JSON.parse(saved);
              items.forEach((item) => {
                const step = item.getAttribute('data-step');
                if (state[step]) {
                  const checkbox = item.querySelector('.checklist-checkbox');
                  if (checkbox) {
                    checkbox.checked = true;
                    updateCheckboxVisual(item, true);
                  }
                }
              });
            }
          } catch (e) {
            console.error('Failed to load checklist state:', e);
          }
        }

        // Save state to localStorage
        function saveState() {
          try {
            const state = {};
            items.forEach((item) => {
              const step = item.getAttribute('data-step');
              const checkbox = item.querySelector('.checklist-checkbox');
              if (checkbox && checkbox.checked) {
                state[step] = true;
              }
            });
            localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(state));
          } catch (e) {
            console.error('Failed to save checklist state:', e);
          }
        }

        // Update visual state of checkbox
        function updateCheckboxVisual(item, checked) {
          const checkmark = item.querySelector('.checkmark');
          const customBox = item.querySelector('.checkbox-custom');
          if (checkmark && customBox) {
            if (checked) {
              checkmark.style.opacity = '1';
              customBox.style.borderColor = 'rgb(38, 38, 38)';
              customBox.style.backgroundColor = 'rgb(38, 38, 38)';
              checkmark.style.color = 'white';
            } else {
              checkmark.style.opacity = '0';
              customBox.style.borderColor = '';
              customBox.style.backgroundColor = '';
              checkmark.style.color = '';
            }
          }
        }

        // Handle dark mode for checked state
        function updateDarkMode() {
          const isDark = document.documentElement.classList.contains('dark');
          items.forEach((item) => {
            const checkbox = item.querySelector('.checklist-checkbox');
            const customBox = item.querySelector('.checkbox-custom');
            const checkmark = item.querySelector('.checkmark');
            if (checkbox && checkbox.checked && customBox) {
              if (isDark) {
                customBox.style.borderColor = 'rgb(245, 245, 245)';
                customBox.style.backgroundColor = 'rgb(245, 245, 245)';
                checkmark.style.color = 'rgb(23, 23, 23)';
              } else {
                customBox.style.borderColor = 'rgb(38, 38, 38)';
                customBox.style.backgroundColor = 'rgb(38, 38, 38)';
                checkmark.style.color = 'white';
              }
            }
          });
        }

        // Set up event listeners
        items.forEach((item) => {
          const checkbox = item.querySelector('.checklist-checkbox');
          if (!checkbox) return;

          checkbox.addEventListener('change', () => {
            updateCheckboxVisual(item, checkbox.checked);
            updateDarkMode();
            saveState();
          });
        });

        // Load initial state
        loadState();
        updateDarkMode();

        // Watch for theme changes
        const observer = new MutationObserver(updateDarkMode);
        observer.observe(document.documentElement, {
          attributes: true,
          attributeFilter: ['class']
        });
      })();
    </script>
  </Section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       SECTION 3: SIMPLE NOW, POWERFUL LATER
       ============================================================ -->
  <Section
    heading="Budgeting made simple"
    bg="stone"
  >
    <div class="envelope-section flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-6 md:gap-0 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Left column: text (on mobile: text, then image+button) -->
      <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 space-y-4 text-center md:text-left">
        <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
          A budget is just a written financial plan.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
          Write down your fixed costs, estimate variable costs. Track your spending, adjust your budget and take control of where your money goes.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
          Envelope based budgeting is one of the most popular budgeting methods. Imagine your spending categories as envelopes. At the beginning of the month you put in a certain amount of money, and when it's empty, no more spending for that category.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-500">
          <a href="/budgeting-app" class="underline hover:text-neutral-700 dark:hover:text-neutral-400 transition-colors">Learn more about budgeting and cashflow →</a>
        </p>

        <!-- Mobile only: image + CTA -->
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-4 py-2 md:hidden">
          <div class="envelope-reveal-mobile w-full max-w-[560px] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
            <img
              src="/images/mindful-money-tracking/envelope_budgeting_light.png"
              alt="Envelope based budgeting"
              class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg block dark:hidden"
            />
            <img
              src="/images/mindful-money-tracking/envelope_budgeting_dark.png"
              alt="Envelope based budgeting"
              class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg hidden dark:block"
            />
          </div>
          <a
            href={APP_URL}
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 border-2 border-neutral-800 dark:border-neutral-200 text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-200 text-base font-medium rounded-xl hover:bg-neutral-100 dark:hover:bg-neutral-800 transition-colors"
          >
            Create a budget
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
