            </span>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Forgetting irregular expenses</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            Car insurance, annual subscriptions, gifts, medical bills - they're predictable, just not monthly. Set aside a small amount each month for these "surprise" expenses that aren't actually surprises.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Mistake 4: Setting unrealistic targets -->
        <div class="mistake-card rounded-2xl p-6 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900 shadow-[8px_8px_16px_rgba(0,0,0,0.08),-4px_-4px_12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[8px_8px_18px_rgba(0,0,0,0.5),10px_10px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12),-3px_-3px_6px_rgba(255,255,255,0.08)]">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
            <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-red-100 dark:bg-red-900/30 flex items-center justify-center text-red-600 dark:text-red-400" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 4l8 8M4 12l8-8"/></svg>
            </span>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Unrealistic targets</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            Cutting dining out from $400 to $0 in one month? That's a recipe for failure. Cut to $300 first. Then $200 next month. Gradual, sustainable changes stick. Drastic cuts don't.
          </p>
